    {
      "id": "5a10aab1ac93489dbf7c966f326e32b4c508efc5",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 462072827,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Looks good.\n\nSMB_COM_TRANSACTION2 was introduced in the Lan Manager 1.2 dialect, and TRANS2_QUERY_FS_INFORMATION was introduced in the Lan Manager 2.0 dialect, so they predate NT and the use of Unicode.\n\n*However*, the SMB_QUERY_FS_ATTRIBUTE_INFO information level was not introduced in that dialect (the documentation I have for that dialect, \"Microsoft Networks, SMB FILE SHARING PROTOCOL EXTENSIONS, SMB File Sharing Protocol Extensions Version 3.0, Document Version 1.11\", doesn't show the information levels; they may have been documented only in the OS/2 documentation), it was introduced in the NT dialect, as per the documentation I have for *that* dialect, \"Portable Systems Group, NT LAN Manager SMB File Sharing Protocol Extensions, August 24, 1992\".\n\nAnd that document says it's always Unicode - not surprising given that NT is Unicode-based.\n\nSo there's no indication that any older servers would send back anything other than Unicode.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
